vAuth Debian packaging
======================

The canonical Debian metadata is kept in packaging/debian/vauth-0.1.0 so that
other distribution formats and versions can live beside it. Debian tools
require this directory to be named debian at the source-tree root.
build-local.sh creates a temporary clean source tree and performs that mapping
without modifying the checkout.

Static Slint prerequisite
-------------------------

The binary package links Slint 1.19.0 statically so installed systems do not
need a Slint runtime package. The local builder must provide the Slint 1.19.0
C++ SDK built with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF and its matching compiler, then set
VAUTH_SLINT_DIR to the directory containing SlintConfig.cmake, for example:

  VAUTH_SLINT_DIR=/opt/slint-static/lib/cmake/Slint \
    packaging/debian/vauth-0.1.0/build-local.sh

Slint is intentionally not listed as a Debian Build-Depends while no suitable
Debian package exists. Consequently this initial packaging is suitable for
local beta packages and a controlled project repository, but it is not yet a
self-contained Debian archive source package.

Distribution licensing
----------------------

The three JSON animation documents under client/assets were downloaded as
public LottieFiles animations and are distributed under the Lottie Simple
License. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md records the known creators, sources, and the
applicable terms. The original page for pending.json was not retained; its
download name was vault.json and attribution is not required by the license.

A statically linked vauth-ui incorporates Slint 1.19.0 under GPL-3.0-only. The
vAuth source remains MIT-licensed, but the combined vauth-ui binary is
distributed under GPL-3.0-only. A public binary distributor must provide the
complete GPLv3 license and corresponding source for Slint 1.19.0, including
applicable notices and source for statically incorporated dependencies. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the Debian copyright file.
